1
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,150
Koichi?

2
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:08,100
I'm over here, Koichi.

3
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:11,200
Rohan Kishibe!

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,988
Now, now, you don't
have to be so defensive.

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:17,400
My days of causing you harm
are long past. Besides,

6
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,797
after reading your history
with Heaven's Door,

7
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:23,351
I found myself filled with a
deep sense of respect for you.

8
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:26,284
I'd go so far as to say
we're two peas in a pod.

9
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:27,658
Wouldn't you agree?

10
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:32,537
now then i'd like to ask
you a question if i may

11
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:35,217
you see i used to call
this area around here my

12
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,357
home until i was four
or so i've spent the day

13
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:41,337
trying to find my old
residence nostalgia must have

14
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:43,917
gotten the better of me
recalling one's childhood

15
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,397
is central to a manga
artist's work however those

16
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:49,777
memories belong to a
four-year-old so they're

17
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:53,460
a little bit foggy oh that's
why i I need your help.

18
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,617
My question concerns this town map.

19
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:57,297
There's something odd about it.

20
00:00:57,380 --> 00:00:59,615
Look, this is the Soba Shop, Ariskawa,

21
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:03,320
Caesar Drugstore, and the
Ocean Convenience Store.

22
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:05,284
They're situated right to left.

23
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,157
Now, take a look at the shops themselves.

24
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:14,017
From the right, you can see Ariskawa,
Caesar Drugstore, and then...

25
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:18,500
You have Ocean on the far
left. See? Huh? That's weird.

26
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:21,477
The map doesn't show a road
between Ocean and the drugstore.

27
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:23,380
What sloppy work?

28
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:25,607
Koichi, would you tag along?

29
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:29,740
I would be forever in your debt if
you'd be my guide for a bit. Huh?

30
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:32,760
Well, I'd like to, but the thing is...

31
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:36,580
That's the response you give
after I ask so politely?

32
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,453
Fine, have it your way.

33
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:42,457
I didn't realize showing me around for
a few meters would be such a burden.

34
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:44,100
He sure is self-centered.

35
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:48,300
I can only spare five
minutes, okay, Sensei?

36
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:57,960
Strange, isn't it?

37
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:01,777
I'm checking my official Chan
press ultra-detailed map of Mariah,

38
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:04,157
and it makes no mention
of this street existing.

39
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,437
On the bright side, since
your map had an error,

40
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:09,461
you might get a gift
certificate at the bookstore.

41
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:19,997
Blast it, this map is absolutely useless.

42
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,440
Take a look, Koichi.

43
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:25,172
It doesn't show the Yonimori,
Honma, or Onodera residence.

44
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,937
There are mistakes everywhere.

45
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:30,417
The bookstore is going to owe me more
than two or three gift certificates.

46
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:33,794
Rohan-sensei, this place looks
like it's been abandoned.

47
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,177
What a weird area.

48
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:42,757
The few houses that are around
here look completely unoccupied.

49
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:45,958
And look, even the vending
machines are out of order.

50
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:47,550
What the?

51
00:02:47,633 --> 00:02:48,620
It's the mailbox.

52
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:53,019
We made our first turn at this corner
when we came down the alleyway.

53
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:56,720
This is too weird.

54
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:59,817
Somehow we've managed to end
up right back where we started.

55
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,360
But we turned right, left, then right.

56
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:04,897
Keep your guard up.

57
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:08,157
There could be an enemy nearby,
manipulating things with their stand.

58
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:09,070
You think?

59
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:12,791
If you would, have Reverb fly
overhead and search the area.

60
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:13,977
Yeah, of course.

61
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:16,697
From up there, I can
see where we need to go.

62
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:17,721
Reverb, act one.

63
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:24,839
What's the matter?

64
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:26,780
There was something up there.

65
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:30,219
I don't know what, but
something just graced Reverb.

66
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:31,460
Are you sure?

67
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:32,797
I didn't see anything.

68
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,457
I know something came
into contact with Reverb.

69
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,200
Excuse me, are you too lost?

70
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,777
I would be happy to be your guide.

71
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:45,100
A girl?

72
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,221
She must be the enemy stand user!

73
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:49,990
Heaven's door!

74
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:54,680
And with a flick of a
finger, victory is mine!

75
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:02,320
We should be safe now.

76
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:06,277
I've written commands in her pages,
so she won't be able to harm us.

77
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,831
Sensei, that was amazing!

78
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:10,277
It's like you launched
your drawing into midair!

79
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:12,717
I've made quite a lot of
progress with my stand.

80
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:13,680
That said,

81
00:04:13,980 --> 00:04:16,097
it still doesn't work on
haters like Josuke who

82
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:18,397
wouldn't know art if it
kicked him in the groin.

83
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,656
She and I are on the same wavelength.

84
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:22,350
Oh, dear.

85
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:25,260
She's just an ordinary
girl, not an enemy. Huh?

86
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,068
So she's not out to get us?

87
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:28,030
That's right.

88
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,697
You can't conceal anything
from heaven's door.

89
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:33,300
Her name is Reimi Sugimoto, age 16.

90
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:35,900
Her address is 312 Code Daimorio.

91
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:37,637
That's not far from here.

92
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:42,014
She has no boyfriend and her measurements
are 82, 57, and 84 centimeters.

93
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:46,937
There's a mole by her left nipple, and her
first period came at age 11 in September.

94
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:50,257
The first time she kissed a boy, he
rammed his tongue down her throat.

95
00:04:50,340 --> 00:04:52,222
That's just about enough, Rohan!

96
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:54,057
If this girl's not a stand user,

97
00:04:54,140 --> 00:04:57,257
then I refuse to allow you to
read anything else about her life!

98
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:59,164
All right, all right, I get it.

99
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,500
Take it easy.

100
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:04,360
I will forget everything that
has just happened. There.

101
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:07,909
I'd be happy to guide you.

102
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:10,737
Really, this place trips
a lot of people up.

103
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:13,017
Several of these alleys look the same.

104
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,977
Please point us in the right
direction and we'll be on our way.

105
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:16,960
Absolutely not.

106
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:18,837
A simple explanation won't cut it.

107
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,626
I'm your guide, so follow me.

108
00:05:24,640 --> 00:05:25,470
Want one?

109
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:29,580
If you're sure, but you still
have to hold on to the end.

110
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:32,640
Uh-oh!

111
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,750
Better be careful.

112
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:35,500
Some girl is gonna dump you.

113
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:37,270
Really?

114
00:05:37,353 --> 00:05:38,183
Where's your proof?

115
00:05:38,266 --> 00:05:39,560
Poco fortune-telling.

116
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,537
The break tells me all about you.

117
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:43,326
You're majorly self-centered,

118
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:46,317
and you have a habit of pushing
people's buttons, don't you?

119
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:48,157
That's why you're going to get dumped.

120
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,717
Get a load of this, Koichi.

121
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,637
Now we know she's off her rocker.

122
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:53,955
She actually thinks I'm self-centered.

123
00:05:54,060 --> 00:05:56,477
You're about to find out
two can play at this game.

124
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:58,797
Light pink nail polish
means you're afraid of love.

125
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,056
That's very telling.

126
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,847
You often let love slip
through your fingers.

127
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,430
No way.

128
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:10,697
I use psychological prodding over
fortune-telling, but enough about your love life.

129
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:13,074
Something else is weighing on your mind

130
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:25,800
Have you heard the story about this house?

131
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:30,960
It said it was the scene of a murder
15 years ago Did she say a murder?

132
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:32,960
Yes, she did

133
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,605
No one lives in the house now.

134
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:39,380
It's empty. Here's why.

135
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:43,960
This story was told to me
by the old lady next door.

136
00:06:44,660 --> 00:06:46,557
It happened in the dead of night,

137
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:49,857
while the young girl was
sleeping soundly in her bedroom.

138
00:06:49,940 --> 00:06:52,417
She awoke to a strange dripping sound that

139
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,757
seemed to be emanating
from her parents' room,

140
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:56,311
but she couldn't be sure.

141
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:00,620
The sound puzzled her. Daddy! Mommy!

142
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:03,500
she called out, but she
never heard a reply.

143
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:04,990
However,

144
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:10,042
the girl wasn't particularly scared, because
she was accompanied by her trusty dog.

145
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,130
Her dog?

146
00:07:11,213 --> 00:07:13,080
Yes, he was a big guard dog.

147
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:16,217
In the darkness, she'd offer
her hand to him under the bed,

148
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:19,217
and he'd always respond
with a whimper and a lick.

149
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:21,418
Arnold was her constant reassurance.

150
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:24,697
But the dripping that
had stolen the girl from

151
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:27,780
her peaceful slumber
continued for several minutes.

152
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:34,880
Finally she'd had enough her curiosity
drove her to investigate what happened next.

153
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:40,877
She found arnold with his throat slashed

154
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,797
hanging from the coat
rack like an old pelt.

155
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:46,157
The dripping sound was
coming from him the sound

156
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:49,897
of his spilling blood
suddenly she heard a voice.

157
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:52,457
Coming from under her bed your hand is so

158
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,160
sweet and tender
sweetheart whimper whimper.

159
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:58,137
I've already murdered
your mommy and daddy.

160
00:07:58,220 --> 00:08:01,720
And then he attacked the girl,
killing her when she died!

161
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:06,156
Tell me that story was just
your way of joking around!

162
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:08,057
Sounded pretty real, didn't it?

163
00:08:08,140 --> 00:08:10,787
You babies, that's for
the nail polish crack.

164
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:16,231
Jeez, my heart can't take stuff like that.

165
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:32,357
That means...

166
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:35,860
Yes, the young girl in
the story was yours truly.

167
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:39,120
Arnold and I only exist as ghosts.

168
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:45,040
They're ghosts?

169
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:47,040
It all makes sense now.

170
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:49,717
Heaven's door could only
access her living memories.

171
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,976
This has never happened to me before.

172
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:56,960
The two of you have stumbled upon the
area where I met my end 15 years ago.

173
00:08:58,020 --> 00:09:00,196
I guess we're on the same wavelength.

174
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:04,052
This place is the gateway
between the living and the dead.

175
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,840
Come on, Koichi, run!

176
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:22,730
Huh?

177
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,000
Damn, we're stuck.

178
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:33,977
Keicho, call Reverb.

179
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:35,957
It can give us directions from above.

180
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:39,317
She must have been the one who
made contact with Reverb earlier.

181
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:41,220
Never mind that. Just do it!

182
00:09:44,740 --> 00:09:45,570
What?

183
00:09:45,653 --> 00:09:47,048
A wall appeared in the sky.

184
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,277
No, that's not it.

185
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,497
Reverb's actually touching the ground.

186
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:52,410
Huh?

187
00:09:52,493 --> 00:09:53,323
What in the?

188
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:56,994
I can't believe this, but
you're the one who's floating.

189
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:00,296
There's only one way to truly escape.

190
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:02,080
Anything else is futile.

191
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:04,634
I'm the only one who knows where it is.

192
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,517
This doesn't make any sense.

193
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,897
How the hell do we fight a ghost?

194
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:09,957
Please, whatever you do, don't possess us!

195
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:11,177
Hold on just a minute.

196
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,097
Quit treating me like a vengeful spirit.

197
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:15,117
I haven't done a single
thing to either of you,

198
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:18,357
but somehow you've found a way to
scare yourselves half to death.

199
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:20,377
Listen, I didn't trap you guys here.

200
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:23,777
We're standing between the living
world and the world of the dead.

201
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:24,690
Wait a second.

202
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:26,997
You two hold some kind of power, right?

203
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:29,139
And you said they're called stands?

204
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:31,597
Maybe that's why you're
mixed up in all this.

205
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:33,974
So you're really not here to attack us?

206
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:36,737
You're even more
suspicious than I thought.

207
00:10:36,820 --> 00:10:39,408
I guess I'm proof of
that stone tape theory.

208
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:42,677
Once I became a ghost, I
was bound to this place.

209
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:44,420
I've been here 15 years.

210
00:10:44,660 --> 00:10:47,897
In all that time, I've never stopped
pleading with people to listen.

211
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:49,840
To let me share my story.

212
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:53,097
But you two are the first
to have truly listened.

213
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:57,117
I gave you my word I'd help you get out
of here, so that's what I'm going to do.

214
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:59,257
But after I finish the story...

215
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:00,220
There's more?

216
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:03,220
Now, as I was saying, the murderer.

217
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:07,737
Before I got a look at his face, his
knife found its way into my back.

218
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:11,200
It was late and dark, and I
was doing my best to flee.

219
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:15,100
I died, but my killer still lives.

220
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:18,512
He's living his life right here in Mariah.

221
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,898
That's what I've been aching to say.

222
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:24,877
Not only is he in town, he's blended in!

223
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,917
Let's back this specter train up.

224
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,917
Why are you confessing all this to us?

225
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,877
Relax, I'm not asking you to catch him.

226
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:33,177
I just need you to tell someone who will.

227
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:37,157
You can tell the cops or anybody
else you think is up to the task.

228
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,070
Slow down!

229
00:11:38,153 --> 00:11:41,897
Why the hell should that kind of
responsibility fall on our shoulders?

230
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:42,810
Rohan-sensei!

231
00:11:42,893 --> 00:11:45,457
Compose yourself I think it's
best we remain level-headed

232
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:49,117
It's an absolute tragedy I'm sorry
your life was stolen from you,

233
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,417
but that still doesn't explain things.

234
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,737
We find the murderers
so you can get closure?

235
00:11:53,820 --> 00:11:55,697
That all seems rather
pointless, doesn't it?

236
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:58,237
You'd be better off
letting go of this world.

237
00:11:58,320 --> 00:12:00,257
Surely moving on to the
next world would be a

238
00:12:00,340 --> 00:12:03,105
better existence than
haunting these alleyways.

239
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:05,410
Tell me,

240
00:12:05,493 --> 00:12:07,737
do you have any idea
how many innocent boys

241
00:12:07,820 --> 00:12:10,620
and girls have gone
missing from this town? No.

242
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:15,151
Then you should know it's eight
times the national average.

243
00:12:15,720 --> 00:12:17,400
Yes, and it gets even worse.

244
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:20,017
Some are being slaughtered in silence.

245
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:21,540
And he's behind it all.

246
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:22,510
Wait a minute!

247
00:12:22,593 --> 00:12:23,477
You can't be serious!

248
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,877
This is still going on and
no one's done anything?!

249
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:28,372
Hey, you can't just say things like that!

250
00:12:28,460 --> 00:12:30,957
According to this story, you
didn't even see his face!

251
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:32,637
How would you know what's going on?!

252
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:36,237
I know because I see the souls of
his victims dominating the skies!

253
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,555
It's as clear as day!

254
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:41,145
The wounds of those souls
are the same as mine!

255
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:43,240
It's horrifying.

256
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:45,040
That gash is so deep.

257
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:47,997
I can't speak with those
traveling to the other side,

258
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:50,200
but I see them depart over and over.

259
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:54,200
He's fueled by a twisted
obsession, one I know all too well.

260
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:58,160
Mariah has always been my
home, and for fifteen years,

261
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:00,157
it stood in the shadow of murder.

262
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:05,060
It's terrifying, and on a personal
level, it's utterly humiliating.

263
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:07,637
When they finally detain that wild animal,

264
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,937
my cherished Mariah will
have a new reputation.

265
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:13,020
all of Japan will know it
as the home of a monster.

266
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:17,897
But none of that changes the fact that
we have to stop him as fast as possible.

267
00:13:17,980 --> 00:13:20,098
He's preying on someone as we speak.

268
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:21,977
And there's nothing at all I can do?

269
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:24,766
whose life will be ripped
away from them next.

270
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:29,237
You still have blood
pumping through your veins.

271
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,577
If you won't take back
Morio's peace and dignity,

272
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:35,072
then tell me who will and I'll
ask for their help instead.

273
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:40,320
I really hope you've taken
what I've said to heart.

274
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:42,000
I've nothing more to say.

275
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:49,513
Well, I heard you loud and clear, and
I'm shocked no one knows about this.

276
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,372
There has to be something we can do here!

277
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,260
How altruistic, Koichi.

278
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,600
This smells like treble.

279
00:14:04,420 --> 00:14:07,537
Although, this vicious killer could
be a good source of inspiration.

280
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:10,855
It all seems like it'd make
for some interesting manga.

281
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,200
Can we get out if we go this way?

282
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:18,317
Don't buy the good guy act.

283
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,637
It's obvious that he has ulterior motives.

284
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:23,677
And when it comes to trustworthiness,
the guy's shady at best.

285
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:25,642
Did you hear a word I just said?

286
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,299
Then we're agreed.

287
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:30,437
I'll show you how to get to the exit.

288
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:31,600
Huh? The exit?

289
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:32,956
Where do we find it?

290
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:37,037
If you go past the mailbox,
you'll find it on the left.

291
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:37,950
Yeah!

292
00:14:38,033 --> 00:14:39,000
Hey, slow down!

293
00:14:39,200 --> 00:14:40,517
Trust me, you don't want to rush it.

294
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,718
There's a rule to making it through.

295
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:44,502
There's a rule?

296
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:45,870
Yes.

297
00:14:45,953 --> 00:14:50,231
Once you make it past the mailbox,
you'll see the exit about 20 meters away.

298
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,817
No matter what happens around that corner,

299
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:55,537
I need you both to promise me
you'll never look behind you.

300
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:56,460
Why not?

301
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:57,856
What would be there?

302
00:14:58,300 --> 00:15:01,057
That's just the rule for
passing to the next world.

303
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:04,199
Even Arnold understands
something as simple as that.

304
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:08,537
Okay, if a dog can handle it, I guess
there's no reason I wouldn't be able to.

305
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:11,140
And if we do look back, what happens then?

306
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:15,337
Well, putting it in layman's terms, your
souls would be dragged into the next world.

307
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:17,200
Put bluntly, you would die.

308
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,280
But don't worry.

309
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:21,091
It'll be a piece of cake.

310
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:23,157
All you have to do is look forward.

311
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,070
Simple, right?

312
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:35,544
Did you feel something, Koichi?

313
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:39,817
Yeah, when we passed the mailbox, something
flew past our legs and went behind us!

314
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:41,135
Remember, eyes front!

315
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:43,420
Just stay calm and you'll be fine.

316
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:50,840
You feel that, Rohan-sensei?

317
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:54,177
There's some kind of ominous
presence creeping up behind us!

318
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:55,380
Yes, I'm aware.

319
00:15:59,220 --> 00:16:03,632
Something's there I don't know what
but there's something right by my head.

320
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:08,037
Just ignore it there will always be
something trying to make you look back.

321
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:11,057
I know it seems scary
and overwhelming but as

322
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:12,897
long as you don't look
back it can't do anything.

323
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:15,637
To cause you harm there's
something warm and

324
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:18,197
runny oozing down my neck
ignoring this thing's.

325
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:19,857
Gonna be a lot tougher
than you're making it

326
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:22,737
sound almost there go
through the light and.

327
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:23,650
You're home free.

328
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:24,563
What?

329
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:26,820
But I can't take any more of this.

330
00:16:26,940 --> 00:16:28,180
And it's so far away.

331
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:30,300
Let's run for it, Rohan sensei.

332
00:16:30,820 --> 00:16:32,357
Panicking will make it worse.

333
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:33,734
It'll try to trip you.

334
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:38,620
You're safe now.

335
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:40,300
You made it.

336
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:42,900
You can turn around now. Go ahead.

337
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,106
I've never been so terrified.

338
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,030
Thank goodness it's all.

339
00:16:48,113 --> 00:16:49,178
No, that wasn't me.

340
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:50,277
Don't look back.

341
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:52,595
It's trying to get you to turn around.

342
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:53,800
You idiot.

343
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:56,255
Koichi, if only you had waited for us.

344
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:59,317
But this didn't happen when I
came through here by myself.

345
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:00,640
Why'd they trick him?

346
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:07,050
Koichi, no!

347
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:10,477
I don't get it, but if we don't
look, we're good to go, right?

348
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:11,913
You lucked out, Koichi.

349
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:12,922
You're with me.

350
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:14,490
Heaven's door!

351
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:16,497
I'm taking your ability to see.

352
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:17,462
You're welcome.

353
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:24,600
You can calm down, Koichi.

354
00:17:25,740 --> 00:17:27,858
I'll reinscribe your ability to see.

355
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:39,477
The alley between the convenience
store and the drugstore.

356
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:40,442
It disappeared.

357
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:43,131
I'm just glad we're back.

358
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:47,300
I'm afraid this is as far as we go.

359
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:50,361
Well, at least until he's caught.

360
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:52,609
When that finally happens,

361
00:17:52,800 --> 00:17:56,557
Arnold and I will look back, and
we'll be reunited with Mom and Dad.

362
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:59,080
Peace and dignity must return to Morioh.

363
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:01,380
Only then can we find eternal rest.

364
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:05,037
I'll be right here if you ever
want to talk about anything.

365
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:07,061
You two don't be strangers, okay?

366
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:11,480
I'm here if you need me,
little Rohan, Mr. Koichi.

367
00:18:12,420 --> 00:18:16,832
From the bottom of my heart, I want to
thank you for listening to my story.

368
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,880
She had some nerve.

369
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:24,637
Where does she get off
calling me little Rohan?

370
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,560
What an audacious ghost girl.

371
00:18:29,060 --> 00:18:31,537
But still, Reimi Sugimoto.

372
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:35,561
She has an unyielding spirit, and
that's something to be respected.

373
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:37,760
For 15 years,

374
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:39,997
she's waged a fight for the living with

375
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:42,786
nothing but her courage
and trusted companion.

376
00:18:52,380 --> 00:18:54,700
There it is, Reimi, age 16.

377
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:58,117
I never doubted her story, but
it's nice to have evidence.

378
00:18:58,200 --> 00:18:59,520
Ah, we have a visitor.

379
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:04,039
You wouldn't happen to be Rohan
Kishibe, the manga artist, would you?

380
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,089
Sorry, have we met before?

381
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:11,430
Let's see.

382
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:14,177
I'd say you would have been
about four when it happened.

383
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:17,907
It doesn't surprise me you have
no recollection of that night.

384
00:19:18,640 --> 00:19:22,380
So, I'll start by saying your
house was close to theirs.

385
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:26,357
The night of the incident your
parents left home for the evening,

386
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:29,977
apparently there was some urgent
business that needed attention.

387
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:32,937
Your parents and the Sugimoto's
were very close friends,

388
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:36,785
so they left you with them while
they handled matters elsewhere.

389
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:42,020
Rohan, that night, the one that claimed
the lives of the Sugimoto family,

390
00:19:42,420 --> 00:19:44,773
you were there and the only one rescued.

391
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:47,700
I was... there?

392
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:51,020
You were able to survive that nightmare?

393
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:56,217
But once you were in police custody, you
started crying and repeating this sentence.

394
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:59,920
Big Sis Reimi snuck me out
the window and saved me.

395
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:05,700
Reimi risked everything to get you to
safety before the murderer could find you.

396
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:10,180
Now it all makes sense.

397
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:12,282
No wonder she acted so familiar.

398
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:16,260
And I learned something
else, my heaven's door.

399
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:19,780
It can't reveal my distant
memories or personal fate.

400
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:27,100
If you ever find yourself wandering
down this alleyway, a word of warning,

401
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:29,680
you should never, ever look back.

402
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:38,820
I'm telling you, I really met a ghost!

403
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:41,177
The girl you saw in that
picture is me dreamy!

404
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:43,097
I already said that we believe you.

405
00:20:43,180 --> 00:20:44,062
Right, Okuyasu?

406
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:46,160
This Code is just my type.

407
00:20:46,320 --> 00:20:48,614
If only I'd been born 15 years earlier.

408
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:52,637
If she's gonna stick around, we should
probably meet your ghost friend too.

409
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:54,097
But fair warning, Koichi.

410
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:55,680
If we go to Jotaro or Mr.

411
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:59,577
Joseph about all this, you can bet your
ass they'll have one question for you.

412
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:00,880
This unknown killer.

413
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:03,139
Is he using a stand on his victims?

414
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:05,440
Uh, I guess.

415
00:21:05,620 --> 00:21:06,796
I really don't know.

416
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:09,597
Well, in that case, it's up
to the police and courts.

417
00:21:09,680 --> 00:21:10,860
What are you saying?

418
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,337
There's a bloodthirsty
murderer loose in Morioh!

419
00:21:13,420 --> 00:21:14,479
Yeah, I know that.

420
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:17,457
And I'm telling you that Jotaro
and the Speedwagon Foundation

421
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:21,237
aren't going after an ordinary
killer no matter how twisted he is.

422
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,700
Now take a deep breath.

423
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:24,877
He's managed to avoid
the police for over a

424
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:26,797
decade and they're
supposed to be the best.

425
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:28,417
It's not like we're
going to summon him like

426
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:31,147
waving down some taxi
by force of will alone.

427
00:21:31,920 --> 00:21:34,997
Let's stay calm and take
things slowly and carefully.

428
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:37,380
So, what did ol' Rohan have to say?

429
00:21:38,960 --> 00:21:45,900
He said the same thing as
you, Josuke Be careful,

430
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:49,060
Koichi You have to be alert
when you cross the road

431
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:50,940
I'm sorry for the trouble

432
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:04,600
Mariah used to be a summer
escape for samurai I know,

433
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:09,077
such an out-there concept might be hard to
believe But my ancestors were among them.

434
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:11,597
We were ruined during
my grandfather's time.

435
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:14,397
All I have left is the house
that I currently live in.

436
00:22:14,480 --> 00:22:16,820
Oh, and my miserable little office job.

437
00:22:19,580 --> 00:22:23,017
Hey, what happened to that nice
imported watch I bought you?

438
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:23,930
That's right.

439
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:25,217
You left it in your bag.

440
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:26,418
How could I forget?

441
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:29,097
If I remember correctly,
I was loose on you.

442
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:30,592
We'll fix that tomorrow.

443
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:41,250
Hmm?

444
00:22:41,333 --> 00:22:42,163
What's wrong?

445
00:22:42,246 --> 00:22:44,315
Why are you being coy all of a sudden?

446
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:46,898
Now, watch your step as you get out.

447
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:49,340
Let's head inside.

448
00:22:49,600 --> 00:22:51,953
A sublime weekend is beyond those doors.

449
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:54,600
It'll be our getaway.

450
00:23:01,560 --> 00:23:03,325
Look at this, you're tripping.

451
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:05,477
Not at all becoming of a lady.

452
00:23:05,560 --> 00:23:07,800
I expect you to clean this up.

453
00:23:13,420 --> 00:23:17,008
I can't recall your name, but
in the long run does it matter.

454
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:19,200
And brava, it's all clean.

455
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:21,562
You should be proud of yourself.

456
00:23:22,780 --> 00:23:23,820
Now then...

457
00:23:24,560 --> 00:23:26,619
I think we should make some dinner.

458
00:23:27,040 --> 00:23:29,393
What's the best dish in your repertoire?
